---
description: Establish the actual owned integration selection and quiet credential readiness relevant to the user's request.
args:
  goal: string
returns: ApiReadinessResult
---
Discover the owned integration inventory through workspace.discoverIntegrationReview. Investigate its authorizing selection with observeIntegrationSelection, passing the actual goal, index and workspace.readIntegrationSelection as a scoped asynchronous reader. Preserve authentic source receipts and distinguish an owner selection from a copied, foreign or obsolete record. Use chooseIntegrationProfile with the goal, inventory and observed history to resolve the actual intended identity. An exact current owner selection can distinguish otherwise identical profile names. Check that identity and relevant earlier/current evidence with checkIntegrationSelection.

When native selection and scope permit a quiet review, open its exact current selection through workspace.openQuietIntegrationPlan. Use reviewQuietCredentials to examine the sealed audience, transport, existing authorization and lifecycle metadata. Preserve the actual native audit through workspace.readQuietIntegrationAudit. If the selection, native plan or lookup is refused, retain that absence and explain what could be established; no guessed readiness or silent replacement selection.

Use decideApiReadiness to interpret what the observations mean for the actual goal. A grant to retain a note does not request one. Distinguish a requested read-only explanation, an explicitly requested local artifact and a conditional artifact whose condition may remain unproven. Stage only the requested permitted finding through workspace.stageIntegrationReadiness with its actual plan, review, audit and null initial handoff. Preserve its real receipt or refusal and return applicationResult with the actual explanation and native evidence. Provider access remains untested: do not connect, send, fetch, publish, refresh, exchange a token or acquire a new grant.
